    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'pride' (concept-core-pride) refers to the general concept of pride, which can encompass positive feelings of satisfaction/dignity, or negative feelings of arrogance. The Japanese expression '自尊' (jison) primarily means 'self-respect' or 'esteem', and while it can be a form of 'self-pride', it is significantly narrower than the general English 'pride'. It does not cover 'pride in achievement' or 'arrogance'. A more natural and common Japanese term for the general positive sense of 'pride' would be '誇り'.",
