      "surface": "誇り",
      "reading": "ほこり",
      "reason": "'誇り' (hokori) is a more natural and common translation for the general positive sense of 'pride', encompassing dignity, honor, and satisfaction in achievement, which '自尊' (self-respect) does not fully cover. It aligns better with the core concept of 'pride' for a general learner."
